# {{name}}

This app runs inside NathApp, which starts it and shows it in a live preview.

- **Commands** are in `nathapp.json`: NathApp installs dependencies, runs `dev` while you work (it reloads on changes) and `build` + `start` when the user is done. Don't start servers yourself; use NathApp's `restart_app` tool after changing dependencies or nathapp.json.
- **Environment** (set by NathApp): `PORT` (listen on 127.0.0.1:$PORT), `DATABASE_PATH` (SQLite file; also as `DATABASE_URL=file:…`), `NATHAPP_FILES_DIR` (a folder for stored files), `NODE_ENV`.
- **Data** is kept by NathApp outside the project folder, so it survives rebuilds and resets: always use `DATABASE_PATH` and `NATHAPP_FILES_DIR`, never data files in the project. The user can browse, export and delete it in NathApp. Other apps' data (same workspace, read-only, after the user allows it): `GET $NATHAPP_API_URL/data`, `/data/<appId>`, `/data/<appId>/<table>?search=&limit=&offset=&order=&desc=1&where.<column>=` with `Authorization: Bearer $NATHAPP_API_TOKEN`, from the server only.
- **Design tokens** live in `src/tokens.css` (colors, radii, fonts, spacing as CSS variables). Style everything with them so the app matches the user's theme.
- **Realtime**: after writing data, call `realtime.publish(topic)` on the server; clients `subscribe(topic, fn)` from `src/live.ts`.
- **AI**: `src/ai.ts` lets the server ask a model (`ai.chat`, `ai.json`, `ai.stream`). NathApp answers with the user's own AI subscription, so there are no API keys. Server-side only: never expose `NATHAPP_AI_TOKEN` to the browser; the frontend calls the app's own API. Requests count against a daily limit, so don't call AI in loops or on every page load, and cache results in the database where it makes sense. Handle `AiError` (e.g. 403 when the user turned AI off, 429 at the limit) with a friendly message.
- **Actions and tools**: list the app's main tasks in `nathapp.json` `"actions"` so the user can run them from NathApp's command bar (Ctrl+K), and agents and other apps from NathApp's tool registry. `{ "id", "title", "input"?, "params"?, "endpoint" }` actions get a POST with JSON `{ input, params }` (header `X-NathApp-Caller`) and answer JSON `{ message, … }`; `{ "id", "title", "path" }` actions open the app at that page. NathApp also derives `list-/get-/add-/update-/delete-<table>` tools from the data (`"dataTools": "read"` or `"none"` turns them down; an action with the same id replaces one). Other apps' tools: `GET $NATHAPP_API_URL/tools`, `POST $NATHAPP_API_URL/tools/<appId>/<toolId>` with `{ params?, input? }` (the user is asked first).
- **Background runs**: NathApp's `create_schedule` tool runs one of the app's actions (or a command) once, on a cron schedule or on an event, even with no tab open. The app can send its own events: `POST $NATHAPP_API_URL/events` with `{ "name": "new-order" }` (server only, `Authorization: Bearer $NATHAPP_API_TOKEN`).
- **Secrets** (API keys, passwords) come from NathApp as environment variables: read `process.env.NAME` on the server only. Never hardcode them, write them to files, log them or send them to the browser. Missing ones are requested with NathApp's `request_secret` tool.
